//RS /// Walk the bundle: flag a `#Target(OS.*)`-gated impl whose enclosing file/
//RS /// module also carries a web-bucket ceiling (`#Target(Wasm)`/`#Target(JS)`)
//RS /// — a structural conflict between the two mutually-exclusive axes
//RS /// (E-OSTARGET-MIXED-AXIS) — and flag a function/method that isn't itself
//RS /// gated to match but takes or returns a value of a gated type
//RS /// (E-OSTARGET-UNMATCHED-CALL): reachable from any build, it would call a
//RS /// method the gated `impl` supplies — a Rust compile error (unresolved
//RS /// method) on every OS but the gated one, since codegen strips that `impl`
//RS /// entirely there (`Codegen/Imports.rs::emit_program_items`). Catching it in
//RS /// sema turns that would-be rustc ICE (I2) into a Jet-level diagnostic.
//RS ///
//RS /// Signature-level, not a full call-graph walk: mirrors how
//RS /// `WebPartition::check_abi_export` also only inspects param/return types,
//RS /// never call bodies. The existing effect call-graph (`fx_edges`) only
//RS /// records bare-name calls (`CheckerInfer/calls.rs`), never method calls, so
//RS /// it can't see a caller reaching a gated `impl`'s methods either way.
